   }
  ],
  "method": [
   "Preferred roster language = a non-English language only for residents who speak English less than 'very well' (limited English proficiency, LEP); everyone else (English-only, or bilingual 'very well') is 'en'.",
   "es, zh, vi come straight from C16001 at city level. ht and pt are C16001's collapsed groups ('French, Haitian, or Cajun'; 'Other Indo-European') times the Haitian / Portuguese share of that group in the city's PUMA(s) from B16001.",
   "LEP residents who speak a language the tool doesn't support yet are left out of the roster mix and reported per city as unsupported_lep_share_of_pop.",
   "City weights = Medicaid/means-tested public coverage among adults 19-64 (C27007).",
   "p_subject_to_requirement = MassHealth's share of renewals NOT completed ex parte (a form was needed).",
   "target_p_lose_given_subject = procedural terminations / renewals that needed a form; the generator solves the latent model's intercept so the expected label rate among subject members matches it."
  ],
  "caveats": [
   "Unwinding renewals (2023-24) are a proxy for the 2027 community-engagement verification, not the same process.",
   "Procedural terminations include some people who were in fact ineligible, and some who were reinstated later; CMS data can't separate them, so the label rate is an upper-bound proxy for 'eligible but lost to paperwork'.",
   "ACS language and English ability cover all residents 5+, not MassHealth members specifically; Medicaid adults are likely more often LEP, so the language mismatch rate is probably conservative.",
   "PUMAs used for the Haitian/Portuguese split include neighbouring towns for Lawrence (Andover), Chelsea (Revere, Winthrop), New Bedford and Fall River. ACS estimates for small groups carry wide margins of error."
  ]
 },
